# Before this fix, selecting this later file rejected the preceding declaration:
# template<S set>:
#     have copied set = S
# with "a template declaration cannot be replayed as a preverified template body".

# Now the trusted prefix reconstructs the template's checked generic Result,
# and the verified target can instantiate it normally.
\prefix::copied<R> = R

# Boundary: preverified template instance bodies still cannot introduce a
# nested template declaration, and duplicate template names still fail.
